NAME
       pci_list, usb_list - enumerate devices

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int cervus_pci_list(cervus_pci_device_t *out, int max);
       int cervus_usb_list(cervus_usb_device_t *out, int max);

DESCRIPTION
       Reports the PCI devices the kernel found, each with its address,
       class, vendor and device id, base address registers, interrupt
       line and MSI and MSI-X capabilities; and the USB devices behind
       the EHCI, UHCI and xHCI controllers.

       Useful when a driver has not bound: comparing the list against
       the kernel log shows whether the device was seen but rejected,
       or never enumerated at all.

RETURN VALUE
       The number of devices written, or negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       lspci(1), lsusb(1), dmesg(1)
